-- ============================================================================
-- D1 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Oilfield Data Quality, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/dataqc/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: IS THE DATA FIT TO USE. A flag is a rule that fired,
-- with its reason. Missing is null, undefined or NaN, and a sentinel such as
-- -999.25 is a present value; completeness, gap runs and the coverage of an
-- interval; definitional range limits keyed by unit, plausibility ranges the
-- caller supplies, units never converted, negative rates and rates while shut
-- in; the depth and time index; a cumulative against its last present value,
-- water cut on a liquid basis, parts that add to a total, frozen runs; well
-- names after a stated normalisation and the digit rule. Digest sections 1 to
-- 16, and section 32.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A check is only as good as its stated
-- convention: a sentinel reads complete, a tolerance tighter than the
-- reporting precision flags every rounded value, and a step equal to maxStep
-- covers. The Associate capstone grades six Associate quantities and grades no
-- outlier statistic and no chart.
-- ============================================================================

values ('dataqc', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-data-quality-means","title":"What Data Quality Means","lesson_keys":["l01-a-rule-a-flag-and-a-reason","l02-the-five-dimensions","l03-what-missing-means","l04-the-sentinel-that-is-present","l05-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-is-it-there","title":"Is It There","lesson_keys":["l01-completeness-and-the-null-fraction","l02-gap-runs","l03-coverage-of-an-interval","l04-a-step-too-long-is-a-hole"]},{"key":"m03-is-it-valid","title":"Is It Valid","lesson_keys":["l01-definitional-limits","l02-plausibility-ranges-are-yours","l03-units-are-never-converted","l04-a-fraction-written-in-percent","l05-negative-rates-and-rates-while-shut-in"]},{"key":"m04-the-depth-and-time-index","title":"The Depth and Time Index","lesson_keys":["l01-a-duplicate-is-any-earlier-value","l02-reversals","l03-the-expected-step","l04-irregular-steps"]},{"key":"m05-does-it-agree-with-itself","title":"Does It Agree with Itself","lesson_keys":["l01-a-cumulative-never-falls","l02-water-cut-on-a-liquid-basis","l03-parts-that-add-to-a-total","l04-frozen-values"]},{"key":"m06-names-and-one-dataset","title":"Names, and One Dataset End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-normalising-an-identifier","l02-near-duplicates-and-the-digit-rule","l03-one-dataset-every-check","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
